# Normalize line endings across platforms. Discovered during tasks.md
# 16.5's local-dev verification: on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`,
# infra/localstack/init/*.sh gets checked out with CRLF line endings; since
# docker-compose.yml bind-mounts that directory straight into the
# LocalStack container (no build-context normalization step), the CRLF
# bytes reach `bash` unchanged and break `set -euo pipefail` parsing
# ("invalid option name") -- every init script silently failed (exit 127
# from LocalStack's own script runner) with no obvious link back to line
# endings. Shell scripts specifically MUST stay LF; text files in general
# get git's usual auto-detection.
* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
